      <p class="eyebrow">Why homeowners open a HELOC</p>
      <h2>Your equity, ready when you need it</h2>
      <p>A HELOC is a revolving line secured by your home. You draw what you need, when you need it, and pay interest only on what you use.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reasons">
      <div class="reason"><h3>Renovate or add on</h3><p>Kitchens, roofs, impact windows, a pool or an in-law suite. Draw in stages as contractors bill.</p></div>
      <div class="reason"><h3>Clear credit card balances</h3><p>Roll scattered card and personal-loan balances into one line you control.</p></div>
      <div class="reason"><h3>Keep your first mortgage</h3><p>A HELOC sits in second position, so the first mortgage you already have stays untouched.</p></div>
      <div class="reason"><h3>Build a safety net</h3><p>An open line can cover a job change, medical bill or hurricane repair without selling investments.</p></div>
      <div class="reason"><h3>Buy your next property</h3><p>Use equity toward a down payment on a rental, a second home or a lot to build on.</p></div>
      <div class="reason"><h3>Tuition and big life moments</h3><p>College costs, a wedding, or funding a business idea, drawn only as each bill comes due.</p></div>
